WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:05.690
It's a day these children will remember all
their lives.

00:00:05.690 --> 00:00:10.290
For many, it's their first time aboard an
aircraft.

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:12.540
But this plane won't be taking off.

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:18.350
"The flight to nowhere" is an airline with
a difference.

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:23.380
It offers passengers a taste of flying without
ever leaving the ground.

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:25.000
Many schoolchildren here are poor.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:28.520
Their families cannot afford a real ticket.

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:31.689
The passengers are treated to a full in-flight
experience.

00:00:31.689 --> 00:00:36.479
They receive boarding cards, safety briefings.

00:00:36.479 --> 00:00:38.949
Even refreshments are served on board.

00:00:38.949 --> 00:00:40.960
It's an eye opening experience.

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:43.640
"I've seen planes in the sky.

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:45.479
I used to think they were really small.

00:00:45.479 --> 00:00:47.789
But now I know they're actually huge...

00:00:47.789 --> 00:00:51.570
"
"I now want to fly to London.

00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:55.449
I've heard there are beautiful things to see
in that city."

00:00:55.449 --> 00:00:59.789
Some lucky passengers even get to visit the
cockpit.

00:00:59.789 --> 00:01:05.210
The man behind the project is Bahadur Chand
Gupta, a retired aircraft engineer.

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:11.910
He sold his land and bought the decommissioned
Airbus A 300 back in 2003 for 600-thousand

00:01:11.910 --> 00:01:16.420
rupees – that's about seven thousand euros
— a real bargain.

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:21.280
He charges people according to what they can
afford — as little as a few euro cents or

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:23.520
even nothing at all for the very poor.

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:26.840
"I belong to a very small village.

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:31.759
And, I never expected that I will become an
engineer and I'll be in the airline.

00:01:31.759 --> 00:01:36.200
And, people from my village they used to say
we want to see the aircraft and they were

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:37.759
not able to see the aircraft.

00:01:37.759 --> 00:01:43.979
And that was the basic idea and basic motivation
that I want to show this aircraft to the poor

00:01:43.979 --> 00:01:47.560
people"
"Air travel remains a luxury for many people

00:01:47.560 --> 00:01:48.560
in India.

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:53.700
For those, who may never get to take a flight,
this comes close to the real thing without

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:54.700
leaving the ground.

00:01:54.700 --> 00:01:59.299
And, it isn't the only place for it in Delhi."

00:01:59.299 --> 00:02:05.770
Not far away, a busy main road that runs parallel
to the runway of Delhi's international airport.

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:10.929
It's the perfect spot in the evening to watch
planes land.

00:02:10.929 --> 00:02:14.220
Trees double up as chairs.

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:17.790
It's all about getting the right vantage point.

00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:23.330
For the poor migrant workers here, shelling
out 4,000 rupees or 50 euros for a cheap flight

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:26.380
ticket is beyond their means.

00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:31.180
"It’s my dream to someday take a plane and
fly to my village in Bihar.

00:02:31.180 --> 00:02:36.019
But that’s only if I manage to scrape enough
money for a ticket."

00:02:36.019 --> 00:02:44.220
Further on, at a railway crossing, regulars
here swear that this is the closest you can

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:49.280
get as the turbojets take off.

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:55.680
"In my village, the planes fly really high
up in the sky.

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:57.939
But from here you can see them up close.

00:02:57.939 --> 00:02:58.939
It's an amazing feeling."

00:02:58.939 --> 00:03:04.240
"We may not have the money for a plane ticket.

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:10.599
But that doesn't stop us from dreaming about
what it must feel like to be up in the sky."

00:03:10.599 --> 00:03:16.560
Back at the flight to nowhere, passengers
simulate an evacuation to finish the experience.

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:21.939
Rarely has an emergency situation seemed like
so much fun.

